%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ab33a3c0ff697734bbc83271f362c881, type: 3}
  m_Name: MissionIntroductions
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CalculusLabEscape.MissionOnboarding
  cards:
  - key: bridge-power
    title: Your first bridge repair
    screen: Power Core
    instructions: "1. Choose the number chip, then place it in the coefficient slot. Drag it, or click chip then slot. [X] marks your selection.\n\n2. Adjust the exponent with - / +. The expression preview follows your controls. Work out the values from the question.\n\n3. Test repair checks your answer. Retry if needed. Use Next calibration when shown. Complete all checks, then choose Install regulator to apply the repair."
  - key: bridge-numbers
    title: Working with number answers
    screen: Number inputs
    instructions: "1. Read the requested value above each box. Enter a number or a fraction using /, such as 3/7.\n\n2. Tab / Shift+Tab switches available boxes. Enter or Test repair checks your values. Switching boxes preserves your draft.\n\n3. Read the feedback, then edit and retry if needed. Use Next calibration when shown. Finish all checks, then install or continue when prompted. Follow the next device marker."
  - key: bridge-choices
    title: Assembling a repair
    screen: Expression choices
    instructions: '1. Compare the expressions with the calculation in the question.
      Click one to select it; [X] marks your choice.


      2. Test repair checks
      the selected expression. An incorrect choice keeps your accepted work.


      3.
      Apply the accepted repair with the install / continue button. Some mathematical
      steps remain after all three components are installed.'
  - key: bridge-rescue
    title: Complete the rescue
    screen: Rescue
    instructions: '1. All required mathematical steps and the three bridge components
      are now complete.


      2. Click Open crossing / rescue calf to release the
      crossing. Watch the calf reach its mother.


      3. Results appear after
      the rescue. They separate completion, accuracy, support and skill feedback.
      Focused practice is available afterwards.'
  - key: case-overview
    title: Inspect the containment device
    screen: Case overview
    instructions: '1. Open Exponent dial first. Completing it unlocks the remaining
      three modules.


      2. Then choose Wires, Sequence or Pressure in any order.
      Case overview returns here; STABLE marks accepted work.


      3. Complete
      all four modules before using the separate Master Deactivation. The device
      stays powered until that final action. The countdown enters Safety Mode at
      zero; you can keep working.'
  - key: case-dial
    title: Using the integration dials
    screen: Exponent dial
    instructions: '1. Read the integral in the question. Use - / + to adjust the
      raised exponent and divisor separately.


      2. Insert +C toggles the constant.
      Check the expression preview, then use Test dials.


      3. Feedback identifies
      what to review without clearing accepted work. When the module is STABLE, return
      to Case overview to choose another module.'
  - key: case-wires
    title: Connecting the terms
    screen: Wire matching
    instructions: '1. Choose a source, then connect it to a socket. Drag source to
      socket, or click source then socket. [X] marks the selected source.


      2.
      Each connection is checked immediately. Accepted wires lock; incorrect wires
      can be retried. You decide which antiderivative matches each source.


      3.
      After all three wires are accepted, connect one common +C. Then return to Case
      overview.'
  - key: case-sequence
    title: Using the procedure cards
    screen: Symbol sequence
    instructions: '1. Read the question. Put procedure cards into numbered slots
      by dragging, or by clicking a card then a slot. Unaccepted cards can be rearranged.


      2.
      Work through the slots from 1 to 4. Enter the requested value; / enters a fraction.


      3.
      Enter or Run next step checks one step. Accepted cards lock and the input clears
      for the next value. Return to Case overview once STABLE.'
  - key: case-pressure
    title: Controlling the pressure
    screen: Pressure gauge
    instructions: '1. Read the bounds and integrand. Work out the accumulated value
      using the upper and lower bounds.


      2. Use - / + to set the release amount.
      Pull release lever checks your setting. The world gauge follows the result.


      3.
      Retry after feedback if needed. Once STABLE, return to Case overview. No constant
      chip is used for this definite-integral result.'
  - key: case-shutdown
    title: Deactivate the whole device
    screen: Master deactivation
    instructions: '1. All four modules are STABLE. The separate master action is
      now unlocked.


      2. Lift the master switch cover. This opens the protection;
      it does not yet shut down the device.


      3. Click Master Deactivation.
      Power turns off during the shutdown animation, then your results and focused
      practice become available.'
